course: dictionary
lesson: 6591
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word noble is a good example. «The Stute Fish calls the Whale "Noble and generous Cetacean."» Here noble means good, brave and honest, because the fish is praising the whale's fine character.
explain: Now look at «Kings and queens depended on nobles.» Here noble means a person of high rank, such as a lord or a duke. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A lord fits, but a kind character does not.
explain: When a word has several meanings, try each one in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense. Noble can also mean impressive and grand, as in «a noble horse», so always check the clues around the word.
fact: Some words have several meanings, and context tells you which one fits.
fact: «Noble» means good, brave and honest, showing a fine character, as in «a noble deed».
fact: «Noble» can mean belonging to high social rank, such as lords, dukes and princes; «nobles» are these people.
fact: «Noble» can also mean impressive and grand, as in «a noble horse».
fact: In science, «noble gas» is a special term for gases such as helium and neon, which hardly react with anything.
exercise: «The Stute Fish calls the Whale "Noble and generous Cetacean."» What does noble mean here? | Lumpy and rough | Made of gold | *Good, brave and honest | Very slow
exercise: «Kings and queens depended on nobles, money and armies.» In this sentence, who are the nobles? | Soldiers who fight in the army | Stone walls around a castle | *People of high rank, such as lords and dukes | Traders who sell goods in the market
exercise: «The noble horse galloped across the field.» Which meaning of noble fits best? | Very quiet | *Impressive and grand | Hungry | Lumpy
test: In «the Four Noble Truths», which meaning of noble fits best? | *Good, worthy of respect | Lumpy and rough | Very old | Made of metal
test: «Noble gases hardly react with anything.» What does this tell you? | Noble gases taste sweet | *Noble gases rarely join with other substances | Noble gases always burn | Noble gases rust quickly
exam: Read: «The noble knight helped the weak.» Which meaning of noble fits best? | *Good, brave and honest | Lumpy and rough | Belonging to the sea | Hardly reacting with anything
